    "display_title": "feat(formation): the Rust backend owns where units stand",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "feature/unit-store-native-places",
    "head_commit_message": "feat(formation): the Rust backend owns where units stand\n\nSpec 35 step 1c (Decision 142). The native unit store's columns - each\nunit's position, its loose place, its fleeing offset and its flag bits -\nlive on the battle's BodyField by slot (UnitColumnsNative): a column is\none copy, a value one call. BodyFieldSync's points go: the field reads\nwhere each unit stands from its columns, by the flags the sync names. The\nsyncs still name those flags from each unit's own squad's entries, since a\nunit moved between squads can leave a bit behind (recorded in the spec for\nstep 2). A native pass runs on its squads' store's field, and a squad made\nalone gets a store on the engine in use. The field tests move a battle\nonto their field, and restore the store's columns along with the entries.\n\ncheck_function_length now ends a function at a static func.\n\nWaived-by: Decision 142\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D25MB57Z7nmE6u7pDpd3yj",
    "head_sha": "b334a00b6c0ac7e4a9bf090cf145b42878e1bebc",
